"expected":[["Q....","..Q..","....Q",".Q...","...Q."],["Q....","...Q.",".Q...","....Q","..Q.."],[".Q...","...Q.","Q....","..Q..","....Q"],[".Q...","....Q","..Q..","Q....","...Q."],["..Q..","Q....","...Q.",".Q...","....Q"],["..Q..","....Q",".Q...","...Q.","Q...."],["...Q.",".Q...","....Q","..Q..","Q...."],["...Q.","Q....","..Q..","....Q",".Q..."],["....Q",".Q...","...Q.","Q....","..Q.."],["....Q","..Q..","Q....","...Q.",".Q..."]]},{"args":[1],"expected":[["Q"]]},{"args":[7],"expected":[["Q......","..Q....","....Q..","......Q",".Q.....","...Q...",".....Q."],["Q......","...Q...","......Q","..Q....",".....Q.",".Q.....","....Q.."],["Q......","....Q..",".Q.....",".....Q.","..Q....","......Q","...Q..."],["Q......",".....Q.","...Q...",".Q.....","......Q","....Q..","..Q...."],[".Q.....","...Q...","Q......","......Q","....Q..","..Q....",".....Q."],[".Q.....","...Q...",".....Q.","Q......","..Q....","....Q..","......Q"],[".Q.....","....Q..","..Q....","Q......","......Q","...Q...",".....Q."],[".Q.....","....Q..","Q......","...Q...","......Q","..Q....",".....Q."],[".Q.....","....Q..","......Q","...Q...","Q......","..Q....",".....Q."],[".Q.....",".....Q.","..Q....","......Q","...Q...","Q......","....Q.."],[".Q.....","......Q","....Q..","..Q....","Q......",".....Q.","...Q..."],["..Q....","Q......",".....Q.","...Q...",".Q.....","......Q","....Q.."],["..Q....","Q......",".....Q.",".Q.....","....Q..","......Q","...Q..."],["..Q....","....Q..","......Q",".Q.....","...Q...",".....Q.","Q......"],["..Q....",".....Q.",".Q.....","....Q..","Q......","...Q...","......Q"],["..Q....","......Q","...Q...","Q......","....Q..",".Q.....",".....Q."],["..Q....","......Q",".Q.....","...Q...",".....Q.","Q......","....Q.."],["...Q...",".Q.....","......Q","....Q..","..Q....","Q......",".....Q."],["...Q...","Q......","..Q....",".....Q.",".Q.....","......Q","....Q.."],["...Q...","Q......","....Q..",".Q.....",".....Q.","..Q....","......Q"],["...Q...",".....Q.","Q......","..Q....","....Q..","......Q",".Q....."],["...Q...","......Q","..Q....",".....Q.",".Q.....","....Q..","Q......"],["...Q...","......Q","....Q..",".Q.....",".....Q.","Q......","..Q...."],["....Q..",".Q.....",".....Q.","..Q....","......Q","...Q...","Q......"],["....Q..","..Q....","Q......",".....Q.","...Q...",".Q.....","......Q"],["....Q..","Q......","...Q...","......Q","..Q....",".....Q.",".Q....."],["....Q..","Q......",".....Q.","...Q...",".Q.....","......Q","..Q...."],["....Q..","......Q",".Q.....","...Q...",".....Q.","Q......","..Q...."],["....Q..","......Q",".Q.....",".....Q.","..Q....","Q......","...Q..."],[".....Q.",".Q.....","....Q..","Q......","...Q...","......Q","..Q...."],[".....Q.","..Q....","....Q..","......Q","Q......","...Q...",".Q....."],[".....Q.","..Q....","Q......","...Q...","......Q","....Q..",".Q....."],[".....Q.","..Q....","......Q","...Q...","Q......","....Q..",".Q....."],[".....Q.","...Q...",".Q.....","......Q","....Q..","..Q....","Q......"],[".....Q.","...Q...","......Q","Q......","..Q....","....Q..",".Q....."],[".....Q.","Q......","..Q....","....Q..","......Q",".Q.....","...Q..."],["......Q",".Q.....","...Q...",".....Q.","Q......","..Q....","....Q.."],["......Q","..Q....",".....Q.",".Q.....","....Q..","Q......","...Q..."],["......Q","...Q...","Q......","....Q..",".Q.....",".....Q.","..Q...."],["......Q","....Q..","..Q....","Q......",".....Q.","...Q...",".Q....."]]},{"args":[6],"expected":[[".Q....","...Q..",".....Q","Q.....","..Q...","....Q."],["..Q...",".....Q",".Q....","....Q.","Q.....","...Q.."],["...Q..","Q.....","....Q.",".Q....",".....Q","..Q..."],["....Q.","..Q...","Q.....",".....Q","...Q..",".Q...."]]},{"args":[5],"expected":[["Q....","..Q..","....Q",".Q...","...Q."],["Q....","...Q.",".Q...","....Q","..Q.."],[".Q...","...Q.","Q....","..Q..","....Q"],[".Q...","....Q","..Q..","Q....","...Q."],["..Q..","Q....","...Q.",".Q...","....Q"],["..Q..","....Q",".Q...","...Q.","Q...."],["...Q.",".Q...","....Q","..Q..","Q...."],["...Q.","Q....","..Q..","....Q",".Q..."],["....Q",".Q...","...Q.","Q....","..Q.."],["....Q","..Q..","Q....","...Q.",".Q..."]]},{"args":[3],"expected":[]},{"args":[2],"expected":[]},{"args":[5],"expected":[["Q....","..Q..","....Q",".Q...","...Q."],["Q....","...Q.",".Q...","....Q","..Q.."],[".Q...","...Q.","Q....","..Q..","....Q"],[".Q...","....Q","..Q..","Q....","...Q."],["..Q..","Q....","...Q.",".Q...","....Q"],["..Q..","....Q",".Q...","...Q.","Q...."],["...Q.",".Q...","....Q","..Q..","Q...."],["...Q.","Q....","..Q..","....Q",".Q..."],["....Q",".Q...","...Q.","Q....","..Q.."],["....Q","..Q..","Q....","...Q.",".Q..."]]}],"gen":"(r, big) => [big ? 9 : r.int(1, 7)]","hints":["Every row holds exactly one queen. So instead of choosing n squares out of n², choose one column per row.","Go row by row. In each row, try every column that no earlier queen attacks. How can you test that in O(1)?","Keep three sets: used columns, used r + c values (one per ↙ diagonal) and used r − c values (one per ↘ diagonal). Two squares share a diagonal exactly when they share one of those values. Choose, recurse into the next row, then remove from all three sets."],"explain":{"intuition":"<p>The same template, with a lot of <b>pruning</b>. Since no two queens share a row, each row holds exactly one queen, so a node of the tree is \"queens placed in rows 0 to r − 1\" and its children are the safe columns of row r. A branch where row r has no safe column dies right there, which is what makes this fast: for n = 8 the search visits about 2 000 nodes instead of the 16 million ways to put one queen in each row.</p>\n<p>The trick is checking \"safe\" in O(1). Along a ↘ diagonal, row and column grow together, so <code>r − c</code> is constant. Along a ↙ diagonal, <code>r + c</code> is constant. So keep three sets: taken columns, taken <code>r + c</code> and taken <code>r − c</code>. Choosing a square adds to all three, un-choosing removes from all three. Build the strings only when a full board is reached.</p>","steps":["Keep <code>cols</code>, <code>sums</code> (r + c) and <code>diffs</code> (r − c) as sets, and <code>pick[r]</code> = column of the queen in row r.","<code>go(r)</code>: if <code>r === n</code>, turn <code>pick</code> into strings and record the board.","For each column <code>c</code>: skip it if <code>c</code>, <code>r + c</code> or <code>r − c</code> is taken.","Choose: add to the three sets and set <code>pick[r] = c</code>. Explore: <code>go(r + 1)</code>. Un-choose: remove from the three sets.","Call <code>go(0)</code>."],"pitfalls":["Checking only one diagonal direction. Queens at (0, 0) and (1, 1) are caught by r − c, queens at (0, 1) and (1, 0) only by r + c.","Removing the column but not the diagonals when backtracking. Later rows then avoid squares that are actually free, and boards go missing.","Storing <code>r − c</code> in an array without an offset. It is negative for squares above the main diagonal; add <code>n − 1</code> or use a set."],"complexity":{"time":"O(n!) upper bound; the pruning makes it much smaller","space":"O(n) besides the output"}},"solutions":[{"title":"Try every column order","idea":"One queen per row and per column means the placement is an ordering of the columns. Generate all n! orderings and keep those with no shared diagonal.","time":"O(n! · n²)","space":"O(n)","slow":true,"ts":"function queenBoards(n: number): string[][] {\n  const out: string[][] = [];\n  const perm = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i);\n  const ok = (): boolean => {\n    for (let a = 0; a < n; a++)\n      for (let b = a + 1; b < n; b++)\n        if (Math.abs(perm[a] - perm[b]) === b - a) return false; // same diagonal\n    return true;\n  };\n  const go = (k: number): void => {\n    if (k === n) {\n      if (ok()) out.push(perm.map(c => \".\".repeat(c) + \"Q\" + \".\".repeat(n - 1 - c)));\n      return;\n    }\n    for (let i = k; i < n; i++) {\n      [perm[k], perm[i]] = [perm[i], perm[k]];\n      go(k + 1);\n      [perm[k], perm[i]] = [perm[i], perm[k]];\n    }\n  };\n  go(0);\n  return out;\n}","py":"class Solution:\n    def queenBoards(self, n: int) -> List[List[str]]:\n        from itertools import permutations\n        out = []\n        for perm in permutations(range(n)):\n            if all(abs(perm[a] - perm[b]) != b - a for a in range(n) for b in range(a + 1, n)):  # no shared diagonal\n                out.append([\".\" * c + \"Q\" + \".\" * (n - 1 - c) for c in perm])\n        return out","js":"function queenBoards(n) {\n  const out = [];\n  const perm = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i);\n  const ok = () => {\n    for (let a = 0; a < n; a++)\n      for (let b = a + 1; b < n; b++)\n        if (Math.abs(perm[a] - perm[b]) === b - a) return false;\n    return true;\n  };\n  const go = (k) => {\n    if (k === n) {\n      if (ok()) out.push(perm.map((c) => \".\".repeat(c) + \"Q\" + \".\".repeat(n - 1 - c)));\n      return;\n    }\n    for (let i = k; i < n; i++) {\n      [perm[k], perm[i]] = [perm[i], perm[k]];\n      go(k + 1);\n      [perm[k], perm[i]] = [perm[i], perm[k]];\n    }\n  };\n  go(0);\n  return out;\n}"},{"title":"Row by row, with column and diagonal sets","idea":"Place one queen per row. A square is safe if its column, r + c and r − c are all unused. Undo all three on the way back.","time":"O(n!) upper bound, far less in practice","space":"O(n)","ts":"function queenBoards(n: number): string[][] {\n  const out: string[][] = [];\n  const cols = new Set<number>(), sums = new Set<number>(), diffs = new Set<number>();\n  const pick: number[] = [];\n  const go = (r: number): void => {\n    if (r === n) { out.push(pick.map(c => \".\".repeat(c) + \"Q\" + \".\".repeat(n - 1 - c))); return; }\n    for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n      if (cols.has(c) || sums.has(r + c) || diffs.has(r - c)) continue; // attacked\n      cols.add(c); sums.add(r + c); diffs.add(r - c); pick.push(c);\n      go(r + 1);\n      cols.delete(c); sums.delete(r + c); diffs.delete(r - c); pick.pop();\n    }\n  };\n  go(0);\n  return out;\n}","py":"class Solution:\n    def queenBoards(self, n: int) -> List[List[str]]:\n        out, pick = [], []\n        cols, sums, diffs = set(), set(), set()\n\n        def go(r: int) -> None:\n            if r == n:\n                out.append([\".\" * c + \"Q\" + \".\" * (n - 1 - c) for c in pick])\n                return\n            for c in range(n):\n                if c in cols or r + c in sums or r - c in diffs:\n                    continue  # attacked\n                cols.add(c); sums.add(r + c); diffs.add(r - c); pick.append(c)\n                go(r + 1)\n                cols.remove(c); sums.remove(r + c); diffs.remove(r - c); pick.pop()\n\n        go(0)\n        return out","js":"function queenBoards(n) {\n  const out = [];\n  const cols = /* @__PURE__ */ new Set(), sums = /* @__PURE__ */ new Set(), diffs = /* @__PURE__ */ new Set();\n  const pick = [];\n  const go = (r) => {\n    if (r === n) {\n      out.push(pick.map((c) => \".\".repeat(c) + \"Q\" + \".\".repeat(n - 1 - c)));\n      return;\n    }\n    for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n      if (cols.has(c) || sums.has(r + c) || diffs.has(r - c)) continue;\n      cols.add(c);\n      sums.add(r + c);\n      diffs.add(r - c);\n      pick.push(c);\n      go(r + 1);\n      cols.delete(c);\n      sums.delete(r + c);\n      diffs.delete(r - c);\n      pick.pop();\n    }\n  };\n  go(0);\n  return out;\n}"}],"followups":["Return only the number of boards, for n up to 14. How do bitmasks for the three sets speed this up?","The board is symmetric. How could you search only half of the first row and still count every board?"],"related":[],"kind":"function","nEx":3,"nBig":2,"lcTitle":"N-Queens","acc":0.007667730728659936,"co":[["Mastercard",94,0],["TikTok",75,0],["Huawei",67,0],["Zoho",65,0],["Amazon",61,30],["Microsoft",60,90],["Google",59,30],["Bloomberg",56,90],["Adobe",55,0],["Meta",49,90],["Accenture",44,0],["Oracle",41,0],["Infosys",39,0],["Goldman Sachs",36,0],["tcs",36,0],["IBM",35,0]]}